<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38670" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεξ-άγω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lead out</i> an army <i>against</i> the enemy,
				<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>extend, lengthen,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν διήγησιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.855c
				</span></i>
			; esp. <i>discuss at length,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				46.8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινος ἀκριβῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					55.28
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> seemingly
			intr. (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάξιν</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἐ. ἀπὸ σφῶν</span>
			<i>extend the line of battle</i> (by taking ground to right or
			left), <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.71
			</span></i>; of ships, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τῷ πλῷ πρὸς τὴν
				γῆν</span>
			<i>extend his line</i> by sailing towards land, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.52
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>